      "contested": "GEM records Status=operating with EndState/Province=California and EndLocation implying the pipeline still reaches California. It does not. The historic ~700-mile Southern Trails system (converted ARCO Four Corners Line 90, crude-to-gas, Docket CP99-163-000) had two California-touching pieces: a never-activated West Zone (Essex, CA to Long Beach, CA, ~209 mi, certificate later vacated/abandoned by FERC, c. 2004-05) and a California sliver of the East Zone. FERC authorized abandonment-in-place of the East Zone's California-to-Arizona segments (~220 mi) in Docket CP17-__ / the 2018 NOI and 2020 extension order; Phase 1 abandonment completed June 29, 2019 per the operator's compliance filings referenced in the extension notice. Only the ~268-mile New Mexico/Arizona/Utah remainder (sold/transferred to the Navajo Tribal Utility Authority, serving Red Mesa, Kayenta, and Tuba City) is operating today. Per the batch instruction to 'distinguish the eastern segment operates from the pipeline operates': the EASTERN (NM/AZ/UT) segment operates; the pipeline as GEM currently attributes it (reaching California) does not. Status=operating is defensible ONLY if read as 'the surviving NM/AZ/UT segment is operating' -- the California endpoint and any capacity/length figure implying a live California connection is stale.",
