      "contested": "GEM records Owner1 = 'Southern Trails Pipeline Co' at 100%. This is the pre-2016 corporate name and is stale as a complete answer, but the successor picture is genuinely split rather than a single clean substitution: (1) Questar Corporation (parent of Southern Trails Pipeline Co) was acquired by Dominion Energy in 2016; Dominion's Questar Pipeline business (including Southern Trails) was then sold to Southwest Gas Holdings, closing Dec 31, 2021, and the surviving interstate-pipeline entities were rebranded 'MountainWest' effective April 1, 2022 -- a verified press release explicitly names a renamed subsidiary 'MountainWest Southern Trails Pipeline Company.' (2) Separately and earlier, Dominion Energy negotiated to transfer/sell the operating (NM/AZ/UT) segment to the Navajo Tribal Utility Authority (NTUA) starting with a signing ceremony Nov 28, 2017, subject to FERC approval expected in 2018 -- consistent with the 2018 FERC NOI and the 2019-2020 abandonment/extension dockets for the California/Arizona legs. I could not fully reconcile, from public sources in the time available, whether NTUA now owns the surviving pipe outright (with 'MountainWest Southern Trails Pipeline Company' remaining only as an inactive/shell FERC certificate holder for already-abandoned mileage), or whether MountainWest retains ownership/FERC-jurisdictional-carrier status while NTUA operates or holds a lesser interest.",
