  "summary": "P0254 (Southern Trails Gas Pipeline) exists, is correctly classified as a gas pipeline, and is not a duplicate of any other roster row. The batch's flagged status concern is confirmed: the pipeline's California reach (both the never-activated West Zone Essex-Long Beach and the East Zone's California/Arizona legs, ~220 mi abandoned-in-place per 2018/2020 FERC dockets, Phase 1 completed June 2019) is retired; only the ~268-mile New Mexico/Arizona/Utah remainder serving Red Mesa/Kayenta/Tuba City still operates -- Status=operating is defensible only for that surviving segment, and EndState/Province=California is stale. LengthKnown (651.80 km/405 mi) matches no documented configuration of the system (high-severity spec concern, flagged not replaced). Owner1='Southern Trails Pipeline Co' is stale, but the successor picture is genuinely split between a 2022 corporate rebrand ('MountainWest Southern Trails Pipeline Company') and a 2017-initiated transfer of the operating segment to the Navajo Tribal Utility Authority (NTUA) -- flagged as contested rather than resolved to one new owner. Filled ProposalYear=1999 (high tier, primary FERC source) and ConstructionYear=2000/July (medium tier, trade press + corroborating same-docket FERC notice). Corroborated (REFS_ADDED, same recorded values) Diameter=16in, StartYear1=2002, SegmentCost=$100M, and Capacity=87 MMcf/d (medium tier, matches historic FERC design-capacity range). Pressure, FuelSource, and Operator[ref] are UNRESOLVED with notes on what was searched. Of 5 harvested wiki_citations leads, 4 were opened and used (questarpipeline.com via Wayback, ntua.com PDF, powerengineeringint.com dead with no Wayback capture found, lakepowelllife.com); eia.gov/naturalgas/data.php was a generic EIA data-portal link, not pipeline-specific, and was not used as a citation."
